Subject: [PATCH 102/102] =?UTF-8?q?feat:=20beta.12=20=E2=80=94=20allowance?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20warning=20strip=20+=20friendly=20daily-limit=20card?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- NemesisBudgetNotice: dismissible strip above the composer once today's AI
  usage crosses 80% (polls GET /usage every 5 min; per-UTC-day dismissal;
  copy escalates at 100%). Students see the ceiling coming instead of
  meeting it as a red API error.
- The metering proxy's 'Daily token budget reached' 429 renders as a calm
  designed card (what happened, resets at midnight UTC, nothing saved is
  lost, upgrade pointer) instead of the raw HTTP error line. All other
  errors keep the existing red row.
